[[2047,15,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The CODE control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied at pin 3 by the\nbattery from the line for the maxifuse EFI of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               to 2/99\nor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99,  through the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B35</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               to\n2/99 or by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of supplementary fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>The supply controlled by the ignition (15/54)\nreaches pin 8 from the line protected by shunt fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B25</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               to\n2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>Pin 4 is earthed.</p><p>The line leading from pin 6 is a serial\nline leading to engine management unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which is responsible\nfor identifying the key and exchanging codes.</p><p>The control unit is equipped with a self-diagnostic\nunit that may be used by connecting the unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              :\nthis receives signals from pin 5 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through\nthe tester line.</p><p>The self-test system also produces the signal\nfor the &quot;CODE failure&quot; warning light, located in the check\ninstrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , which comes out of pin 2 of the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The check module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a supply\ncontrolled by the ignition (INT) at pin 1 from the line protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               to 2/99 or from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of supplementary fuse\nbox \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99: when this earth signal arrives, the &quot;CODE\nfailure&quot; warning light comes on.</p><p>A second control unit connector is connected\nvia two leads to the aerial, fitted coaxially to the ignition key,\nin order to detect key insertion and rotation.</p>"]]